Antedeluvian previously belonged to [[Vlad Tepes]], a very evil Seeker, and his [[Amulet]] was contained in [[Spear of Vlad the Impaler|Vlad's Spear]], before eventually becoming separated. The Huntik team deduced that Vlad may have put a spell on his Titans to keep them invoked. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

Years later, Antedeluvian attacked [[Lok Lambert]], [[Sophie Casterwill]] and [[Cherit]] while they ventured through the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]]. After defeating [[Icarus]], Antedeluvian pursued the trio but in vain as they escaped through an alcove. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

After some time, Antedeluvian became a more wild and uncontrollable with the Foundation Agents stationed at Vlad's Castle struggling to subdue him. [[Metz]] asked Lok, having experience with controlling wild Titans like [[Lindorm]], to see if he could subdue him and lead the mission [[Vampire Hunter]]. However, unbeknownst to them, the [[Blood Spiral]] had taken an interest in the [[Heart of Vlad Dracul]] and [[Harrison Fears]] had already bonded with Antedeluvian, who then became [[Powerbonded]]. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

Harrison later invoked Powerbonded Antedeluvian whilst [[Tantras]] embarked on a ritual to obtain the power of Vlad Dracul which almost devastating consequences for the Huntik team. Having grown considerably in strength, Antedeluvian defeated [[Lindorm|Powerbonded Lindorm]] in one hit before gaining his ability. With his power further intensified from two [[Marauder]] Titans through Harrison's [[Bloodrank]], he then went on to overpower [[Sabriel|Powerbonded Sabriel]] and [[Kaioh the Tracker]] and fought against [[Sorcerel|Powerbonded Sorcerel]]. When [[Dante Vale]] arrived with [[Ignatius]], Antedeluvian was defeated by the pair with Dante using his new [[Copykind]] power to utilize Ignatius' Burn ability. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

Harrison summoned Powerbonded Antedeluvian against his brother [[Den Fears]] during their final battle at the [[Blood Spiral Base]]. After being hit by a [[Dragonfist]], Antedeluvian recovered and defeated [[Cursed Archer]] with his Life Drain ability. However, when Den Powerbonded with [[Vigilante]], the two merged using his Cindercloak ability and defeated Antedeluvian. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

[[File:S2E43 Lok Antedeluvian Sabriel 2.jpg|thumb|Powerbonded Antedeluvian uses [[Kaioh the Tracker]]'s staff (right hand) after taking him out|175x175px]]
Upon [[Powerbonding]], Antedeluvian gains golden armor, taloned wings, a flexible blade and bat-like mask. Like other Powerbonded Titans his size increased; from being equal in height to Icarus, to being larger than Powerbonded Sabriel and Kaioh. His original Power Drain ability has been strengthened into '''Energy Drain''' which allows  Powerbonded Antedeluvian to gain the energy and abilities of enemy Titans that he hits, allowing to incorporate [[Lindorm]]'s Spinning Attack into his sword, or grab and make use of other [[Titans]]' weapons. {{source|Lok's Leadership}} His other abilities include:

*'''Lifedrain''' - drains a Titan of all their energy. {{Source|Lok's Leadership}}
*'''Swooping Strike''' - enables him to dive forcefully through the air at his opponent whilst wielding his blade. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}
